{"id": "ppp-and-city-money", "title": "Forgiven federal payroll loans went to nonprofits whose City funding was rising", "seconds": 134.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "cea3ccb2071bbb1d", "words": 405, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "In the pandemic, the federal government lent employers money for payroll.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.3, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Paycheck Protection Program", "sub": "federal payroll loans, 2020 to 2021"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.18, 0.76, 0.89, 1.1, 1.52, 1.77, 2.19, 2.48, 2.59]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[0]"], "text": "178 nonprofits the City pays took these loans. How much in all?", "t0": 3.42, "t1": 7.57, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "City-funded nonprofits", "sub": "loans of $150,000 or more"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.4, 0.88, 1.5, 1.59, 1.82, 2.15, 2.45, 2.69, 3.3, 3.58, 3.73, 3.85]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]", "amount"], "text": "264.1 million dollars.", "t0": 7.57, "t1": 11.45, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$264.1 million", "label": "in federal payroll loans", "sub": "$260.4 million was forgiven"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.59, 1.02, 1.74, 2.14, 2.44, 3.22]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.97, "t1": 13.59, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.41, 0.96, 1.16, 1.29]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "260.4 million dollars of it was forgiven, never paid back.", "t0": 13.81, "t1": 17.72, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Forgiven", "chip": "$260.4 million"}, "emph": ["260.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.28, 0.6, 0.88, 1.15, 1.6, 1.91, 2.0, 2.14, 2.33, 3.12, 3.34, 3.6]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "To get one, a borrower had to promise the loan was needed, because times were uncertain.", "t0": 17.84, "t1": 22.17, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "economic uncertainty made the loan necessary"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.27, 0.61, 0.71, 1.06, 1.23, 1.32, 1.71, 1.86, 2.11, 2.26, 2.77, 3.08, 3.5, 3.67]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "But many borrowers were City contractors. Their biggest customer, the City, kept paying.", "t0": 22.29, "t1": 26.73, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "The City kept paying", "sub": "87 of the 178 got more"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.32, 0.78, 0.98, 1.2, 1.96, 2.24, 2.52, 3.03, 3.14, 3.78, 3.99]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "By 2021, 87 got at least ten percent more than in 2019.", "t0": 26.85, "t1": 30.62, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "The City kept paying", "sub": "87 of the 178 got more"}, "emph": ["87"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.24, 0.91, 1.33, 1.51, 1.59, 1.85, 2.0, 2.4, 2.66, 2.86, 2.97, 3.14]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[3]"], "text": "Here's the worry. City contracts pay back real salaries.", "t0": 30.74, "t1": 33.73, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City contract", "sub": "pays back actual salaries"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Federal loan", "sub": "pays salaries, then forgiven"}, {"art": "question", "name": "The same paycheck?", "sub": "invoices are not public"}], "kicker": "Why it matters"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.31, 0.85, 1.14, 1.61, 1.8, 2.02, 2.35]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[3]"], "text": "So if a forgiven loan paid the same salary, that payroll was paid twice.", "t0": 33.85, "t1": 37.66, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City contract", "sub": "pays back actual salaries"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Federal loan", "sub": "pays salaries, then forgiven"}, {"art": "question", "name": "The same paycheck?", "sub": "invoices are not public"}], "kicker": "Why it matters"}, "emph": ["twice"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.17, 0.24, 0.61, 0.93, 1.16, 1.25, 1.47, 2.17, 2.34, 2.86, 3.06, 3.34]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "innocent[1]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "The Controller’s rule, May 2020: never invoice the City for costs the loan paid.", "t0": 37.78, "t1": 42.82, "shot": "b7c", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Controller’s policy, 22 May 2020", "source": "x21a", "text": "Nonprofits must not invoice the City for any costs paid using PPP funds.", "mark": "must not invoice the City"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.01, 0.49, 0.96, 1.14, 1.41, 2.28, 2.56, 2.99, 3.11, 3.42, 3.65, 4.09, 4.29, 4.57]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["innocent[1]"], "text": "But contract budgets could be revised, so rising City pay is weak evidence.", "t0": 42.94, "t1": 46.82, "shot": "b7c", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Controller’s policy, 22 May 2020", "source": "x21a", "text": "Departments may approve contract budget revisions", "mark": "contract budget revisions"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.51, 0.84, 1.11, 1.27, 1.98, 2.11, 2.44, 2.67, 2.93, 3.12, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead is Catholic Charities.", "t0": 47.04, "t1": 48.94, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Catholic Charities", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.31, 0.66, 0.88, 1.28]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "Its loan was approved in April 2020. How big was it?", "t0": 49.06, "t1": 52.12, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Catholic Charities", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.31, 0.46, 0.86, 1.0, 1.33, 1.65, 2.28, 2.51, 2.65, 2.79]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "5.9 million dollars.", "t0": 52.12, "t1": 54.37, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5.9 million", "label": "PPP loans, Catholic Charities", "sub": "forgiven in full"}, "emph": ["5.9"], "wt": [0.04, 0.48, 0.85, 1.09, 1.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Meanwhile, City pay climbed. 14.5 million in 2019.", "t0": 54.89, "t1": 59.29, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Catholic Charities", "approved": "04/06/2020", "city": [["2019", "$14.5 million"], ["2020", "$16.9 million"], ["2021", "$19.1 million"]], "loan": "$5.9 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.48, 0.76, 1.04, 1.82, 2.36, 2.72, 2.9, 3.43, 3.59, 3.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "16.9 million. Then 19.1 million in 2021.", "t0": 59.41, "t1": 64.09, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Catholic Charities", "approved": "04/06/2020", "city": [["2019", "$14.5 million"], ["2020", "$16.9 million"], ["2021", "$19.1 million"]], "loan": "$5.9 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "emph": ["19.1 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.65, 0.91, 1.41, 2.05, 2.52, 2.82, 2.92, 3.36, 3.56, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corporation, a housing group.", "t0": 64.31, "t1": 68.12, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corp", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "affordable housing"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.26, 0.54, 0.73, 1.31, 1.78, 2.25, 3.1, 3.17, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "5.8 million dollars.", "t0": 68.24, "t1": 70.06, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5.8 million", "label": "PPP loans, Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corp", "sub": "forgiven in full"}, "emph": ["5.8"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.5, 0.63, 1.21]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "And its City pay? 4.7 million in 2019.", "t0": 70.58, "t1": 73.91, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corp", "approved": "05/01/2020", "city": [["2019", "$4.7 million"], ["2020", "$7.6 million"], ["2021", "$8.0 million"]], "loan": "$5.8 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.24, 0.47, 1.03, 1.31, 1.59, 1.92, 2.4, 2.56, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Then 7.6 million. Then 8 million.", "t0": 74.03, "t1": 76.45, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corp", "approved": "05/01/2020", "city": [["2019", "$4.7 million"], ["2020", "$7.6 million"], ["2021", "$8.0 million"]], "loan": "$5.8 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "emph": ["8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.32, 0.56, 0.81, 1.52, 1.78, 1.94]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead is the Jewish Community Center of San Francisco.", "t0": 76.67, "t1": 79.49, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Jewish Community Center of SF", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.22, 0.28, 0.41, 0.78, 0.88, 0.98, 1.31, 1.71, 2.02, 2.12, 2.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "It got two loans, in April 2020 and January 2021.", "t0": 79.61, "t1": 83.3, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Jewish Community Center of SF", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.24, 0.42, 1.03, 1.12, 1.37, 1.58, 1.92, 2.34, 2.85, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "5.6 million dollars.", "t0": 83.42, "t1": 85.59, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5.6 million", "label": "PPP loans, Jewish Community Center of SF", "sub": "forgiven in full"}, "emph": ["5.6"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.63, 0.86, 1.45]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Its City pay is small, but it rose too.", "t0": 86.11, "t1": 88.11, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Jewish Community Center of SF", "approved": "04/10/2020; 01/28/2021", "city": [["2019", "$201,315"], ["2020", "$261,994"], ["2021", "$265,757"]], "loan": "$5.6 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.31, 0.5, 0.65, 1.09, 1.24, 1.38, 1.66]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead is Brilliant Corners, which runs housing for people leaving the streets.", "t0": 88.33, "t1": 91.96, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Brilliant Corners", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "supportive housing"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.01, 0.29, 0.55, 0.68, 1.09, 1.66, 1.81, 2.02, 2.41, 2.53, 2.74, 2.99, 3.1]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "3.8 million dollars.", "t0": 92.08, "t1": 93.81, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$3.8 million", "label": "PPP loans, Brilliant Corners", "sub": "forgiven in full"}, "emph": ["3.8"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.5, 0.72, 1.19]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "City pay: 4.2 million, then 4.4 million, then 5.5 million.", "t0": 94.33, "t1": 99.61, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Brilliant Corners", "approved": "04/11/2020", "city": [["2019", "$4.2 million"], ["2020", "$4.4 million"], ["2021", "$5.5 million"]], "loan": "$3.8 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.57, 0.94, 1.24, 1.34, 1.99, 2.19, 2.41, 2.71, 2.87, 3.61, 3.86, 4.1, 4.51, 4.68]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead is Progress Foundation, a mental health group. Its loan came in June 2020.", "t0": 99.83, "t1": 104.76, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Progress Foundation", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "mental health programs"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.32, 0.6, 0.78, 1.18, 1.9, 1.97, 2.23, 2.46, 2.9, 3.25, 3.51, 3.69, 3.81, 4.17, 4.44]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "3.7 million dollars.", "t0": 104.88, "t1": 106.9, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$3.7 million", "label": "PPP loans, Progress Foundation", "sub": "forgiven in full"}, "emph": ["3.7"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.51, 0.76, 1.41]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bars", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "City pay: 18.6 million, then 19 million, then 21.7 million.", "t0": 107.42, "t1": 112.56, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "bars", "orgs": [{"name": "Progress Foundation", "approved": "06/17/2020", "city": [["2019", "$18.6 million"], ["2020", "$19.0 million"], ["2021", "$21.7 million"]], "loan": "$3.7 million", "forgiven": "in full"}]}, "emph": ["21.7 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.77, 1.12, 1.45, 1.64, 2.31, 2.5, 2.78, 3.51, 3.69, 4.12, 4.43, 4.65]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "So why could these groups say they needed the loan?", "t0": 112.78, "t1": 115.24, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "other revenue did collapse"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.32, 0.46, 0.62, 1.0, 1.34, 1.55, 1.87, 2.02]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "Other income, like donations or events, did collapse.", "t0": 115.24, "t1": 118.35, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "other revenue did collapse"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.87, 1.03, 1.55, 1.7, 2.27, 2.43]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Nobody has shown any group billed the same cost to both.", "t0": 118.47, "t1": 121.24, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That anyone charged the same cost to both", "That every name match is right"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.42, 0.71, 0.96, 1.28, 1.52, 1.64, 1.97, 2.26, 2.37]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "And for 9 payee names, the match rests on the name alone.", "t0": 121.36, "t1": 124.85, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That anyone charged the same cost to both", "That every name match is right"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.22, 0.56, 0.9, 1.44, 1.54, 1.9, 2.36, 2.51, 2.64, 3.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it?", "t0": 124.97, "t1": 125.61, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Any Controller review of double-billing in 2020 and 2021"}, {"who": "", "what": "Invoices and forgiveness forms, compared pay period by pay period"}], "focus": 1}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.19, 0.44]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "The City invoices and the loan forgiveness forms, side by side, for the same pay periods.", "t0": 125.61, "t1": 131.11, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Any Controller review of double-billing in 2020 and 2021"}, {"who": "", "what": "Invoices and forgiveness forms, compared pay period by pay period"}], "focus": 1}, "wt": [0.04, 0.48, 0.71, 1.39, 1.66, 1.76, 2.01, 2.51, 3.09, 3.37, 3.56, 4.12, 4.19, 4.31, 4.62, 4.84]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 131.23, "t1": 133.2, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.34, 0.47, 0.54, 1.13, 1.28, 